</TD>
</TR>


<TR style="line-height: 6pt; font-size: 1pt"><TD>&nbsp;</TD></TR>

<TR>
    <TD valign="top">
</TD>
    <TD></TD>
    <TD valign="bottom">
<DIV style="text-indent: -9pt; margin-left: 9pt">
    &#149;&#160;<I>Real Estate Credit Experience</I>&#160;&#151;
    Since the inception of its operations, NorthStar has made 1,138
    investments aggregating approximately $8.85&#160;billion,
    consisting of $1.3&#160;billion of net lease and healthcare real
    estate assets, $4&#160;billion of real estate loan assets, and
    $3.6&#160;billion (face amount) of real estate securities
    investments. As a result of the depth and thoroughness of its
    underwriting process, the extensive investing experience of its
    management team and its strong performance record in managing a
    diverse portfolio of assets, NorthStar has earned a reputation
    as a leading real estate manager, which has allowed it to access
    low cost, match funded financing to efficiently leverage its
    assets.</DIV>
</TD>
</TR>


<TR style="line-height: 6pt; font-size: 1pt"><TD>&nbsp;</TD></TR>

<TR>
    <TD valign="top">
</TD>
    <TD></TD>
    <TD valign="bottom">
<DIV style="text-indent: -9pt; margin-left: 9pt">
    &#149;&#160;<I>Market Knowledge and Industry
    Relationships</I>&#160;&#151; Through its active and broad
    participation in the fixed income markets, NorthStar benefits
    from market information that enables it to identify attractive
    commercial real estate debt investment opportunities and to make
    informed decisions with regard to the relative valuation of
    financial assets and capital allocation. We believe that
    NorthStar&#146;s extensive industry relationships with a wide
    variety of commercial real estate owners and operators, brokers
    and other intermediaries and third party commercial real estate
    debt originators will provide us with a competitive advantage in
    sourcing attractive investment opportunities to meet our
    investment objectives.</DIV>
</TD>
</TR>


<TR style="line-height: 6pt; font-size: 1pt"><TD>&nbsp;</TD></TR>

<TR>
    <TD valign="top">
</TD>
    <TD></TD>
    <TD valign="bottom">
<DIV style="text-indent: -9pt; margin-left: 9pt">
    &#149;&#160;<I>Public Company Reporting</I>&#160;&#151;
    NorthStar&#146;s common stock has been traded on the New York
    Stock Exchange under the symbol &#147;NRF&#148; since October
    2004. Its management team is skilled in public company
    reporting, compliance with the requirements of the
    Sarbanes-Oxley Act of 2002 including internal control
    certifications, stock exchange regulations and investor
    relations.</DIV>
</TD>
</TR>


<TR style="line-height: 6pt; font-size: 1pt"><TD>&nbsp;</TD></TR>

<TR>
    <TD valign="top">
</TD>
    <TD></TD>
    <TD valign="bottom">
<DIV style="text-indent: -9pt; margin-left: 9pt">
    &#149;&#160;<I>REIT Compliance</I>&#160;&#151; NorthStar has
    operated as a REIT since October 2004, and its management team
    is skilled in compliance with the requirements under the
    Internal Revenue Code to obtain REIT status and to maintain the
    ability to be taxed as a REIT for U.S. federal income tax
    purposes.</DIV>
</TD>
</TR>


<TR style="line-height: 6pt; font-size: 1pt"><TD>&nbsp;</TD></TR>

<TR>
    <TD valign="top">
</TD>
    <TD></TD>
    <TD valign="bottom">
<DIV style="text-indent: -9pt; margin-left: 9pt">
    &#149;&#160;<I>Consistent, Attractive Dividends</I>&#160;&#151;
    NorthStar has a history of consistently providing attractive
    quarterly dividends to its stockholders due to the
    income-oriented nature of the majority of its investments, which
    is also the focus of our investment strategy.</DIV>
</TD>
</TR>


<TR style="line-height: 6pt; font-size: 1pt"><TD>&nbsp;</TD></TR>

<TR>
    <TD valign="top">
</TD>
    <TD></TD>
    <TD valign="bottom">
<DIV style="text-indent: -9pt; margin-left: 9pt">
    &#149;&#160;<I>Distribution Support Commitment</I>&#160;&#151;
    In order to provide additional funds to pay distributions to our
    stockholders at a rate of at least 8% per annum on
    stockholders&#146; invested capital before we have acquired a
    substantial portfolio of income-producing investments, NorthStar
    has agreed to purchase up to an aggregate of $10&#160;million
    shares of our common stock during the two-year period following
    commencement of this offering. If our adjusted funds from
    operations, or AFFO, for any calendar quarter is less than an
    amount equal to an 8% cumulative, non-compounded, annual return
    on stockholders&#146; invested capital, prorated for such
    quarter, NorthStar will purchase shares at the end of each
    calendar quarter equal to the amount by which the distributions
    paid to our stockholders during such quarter exceeds our AFFO
    for such quarter. For more information regarding
    NorthStar&#146;s share purchase commitment and our distribution
    policy, please see &#147;Description of Capital
    Stock&#160;&#151; Distributions.&#148;</DIV>
</TD>
</TR>

