<DIV style="margin-top: 6pt; font-size: 1pt">&nbsp;</DIV>

<DIV align="left" style="margin-left: 0%; margin-right: 0%; text-indent: 4%; font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times; color: #000000; background: #FFFFFF">
    If we meet the qualifications established by the FDIC and to the
    extent consistent with our investment objectives, we may
    participate as a private investor in the PPIP, which was
    announced on March&#160;23, 2009 by the U.S.&#160;Treasury in
    conjunction with the FDIC and Federal Reserve. Targeting
    illiquid real estate loans held on the books of financial
    institutions, referred to as legacy loans, and securities backed
    by loan portfolios, referred to as legacy securities, the PPIP
    is designed to open lending channels by facilitating a market
    for distressed assets. Under the Legacy Loans Program, the
    U.S.&#160;Treasury and private investors will invest equity
    capital into individual public-private investment funds, or
    PPIFs, which will be established to own and manage loans and
    other assets from these financial institutions. The FDIC will
    provide a debt guarantee to the PPIFs and will have broad
    oversight for the formation, funding and operation of the PPIFs;
    however, the private investor will control and manage the assets
    in the PPIFs until final liquidation. The PPIP has been
    structured to combine $75 to $100&#160;billion in capital from
    the Troubled Assets Relief Program, or TARP, with capital from
    the private sector to generate $500&#160;billion in purchasing
    power and to improve and stabilize the financial systems. We may
    also invest in any other future government sponsored programs
    for which we qualify to the extent consistent with our
    investment objectives.
</DIV>

<DIV align="left"><FONT size="1">

</FONT></DIV>

<DIV style="margin-top: 12pt; font-size: 1pt">&nbsp;</DIV>

<DIV align="left" style="margin-left: 2%; margin-right: 0%; font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica; color: #000000; background: #FFFFFF">

    <B><I><FONT style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times">Other
    Possible Investments</FONT></I></B>
</DIV>

<DIV style="margin-top: 6pt; font-size: 1pt">&nbsp;</DIV>

<DIV align="left" style="margin-left: 0%; margin-right: 0%; text-indent: 4%; font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times; color: #000000; background: #FFFFFF">
    Although we expect that most of our investments will be of the
