<DIV align="left" style="margin-left: 0%; margin-right: 0%; text-indent: 4%; font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times; color: #000000; background: #FFFFFF">
    NorthStar is a publicly registered, New York Stock Exchange
    listed (NYSE: NRF) company that is internally administered and
    managed and operates as a REIT. NorthStar was formed in October
    2003 to engage in the business of investing in and managing
    commercial real estate debt, commercial real estate securities
    and net lease properties. In October 2004, NorthStar commenced
    its operations upon the closing of its initial public offering
    pursuant to which it issued approximately 21&#160;million shares
    of common stock for net proceeds of approximately
    $170&#160;million. Simultaneously with the closing of
    NorthStar&#146;s initial public offering, NorthStar acquired, in
    exchange for approximately 4.7&#160;million units of limited
    partnership interests in its operating partnership and
    approximately $36&#160;million in cash, certain investments in
    commercial real estate debt, commercial real estate securities
    and net lease properties. As of April&#160;17, 2009, NorthStar
    had 204 record holder&#146;s of its common stock.
</DIV>

<DIV align="left"><FONT size="1">

</FONT></DIV>

<DIV align="left"><FONT size="1">

</FONT></DIV>

<DIV style="margin-top: 6pt; font-size: 1pt">&nbsp;</DIV>

<DIV align="left" style="margin-left: 0%; margin-right: 0%; text-indent: 4%; font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times; color: #000000; background: #FFFFFF">
    As of December&#160;31, 2008, NorthStar has $6.5&#160;billion of
    assets under management consisting of approximately
    $2.1&#160;billion of commercial real estate debt that NorthStar
    has acquired or originated, including first mortgage loans,
    second mortgage loans, mezzanine loans and loan participations;
    approximately $2.1&#160;billion of primarily investment grade
    commercial real estate securities, such as commercial mortgage
    backed securities, fixed income securities issued by REITs and
    credit-rated tenant loans; approximately $0.9&#160;billion
    non-investment grade commercial real estate securities,
    approximately $1.3&#160;billion of office, industrial, retail
    and healthcare-related properties across the United States that
    are net leased long-term to corporate tenants or healthcare
    facility operators, and approximately $0.1&#160;billion of
    equity invested in the middle market lending and residential
    land businesses. NorthStar&#146;s portfolio is diversified by
    investment size, security type, property type and geographic
    region.
</DIV>

<DIV align="left"><FONT size="1">

</FONT></DIV>

<DIV style="margin-top: 6pt; font-size: 1pt">&nbsp;</DIV>

<DIV align="left" style="margin-left: 0%; margin-right: 0%; text-indent: 4%; font-size: 10pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times; color: #000000; background: #FFFFFF">
    NorthStar&#146;s primary investment objectives are similar to
    ours. It seeks to produce attractive risk-adjusted returns and
    to generate predictable cash flow for distribution to its
    stockholders. The profitability and performance of
    NorthStar&#146;s business is a function of several metrics:
    (i)&#160;growth of assets under management; (ii)&#160;growth in
    &#147;adjusted funds from operations,&#148; which is a non-GAAP
    measure of cash flow from operations; and (iii)&#160;overall
    returns realized on invested equity. The credit quality of
    NorthStar&#146;s investments, the diversification of its
    portfolio and the underwriting and portfolio management
    capabilities of the members of NorthStar&#146;s management team,
    who also serve as our advisor&#146;s management team, are
    additional key factors in the performance of NorthStar&#146;s
    business. Since the completion of its initial public offering
    through December&#160;31, 2008, NorthStar has grown its assets
    under management by more than 500%.
</DIV>

