    shares. Accordingly, unless an administrative or statutory
    exemption applies, shares should not be purchased by a Benefit
    Plan with respect to which any of the above persons is a
    fiduciary. A person is a fiduciary with respect to a Benefit
    Plan under Section&#160;3(21) of ERISA if, among other things,
    the person has discretionary authority or control with respect
    to the Benefit Plan or &#147;plan assets&#148; or provides
    investment advice for a fee with respect to plan assets. Under a
    regulation issued by the Department of Labor, a person shall be
    deemed to be providing investment advice if that person renders
